Usage:
  bb tasks update <key-or-id> [--status <backlog|todo|in_progress|in_review|done|canceled>] [--priority <urgent|high|medium|low|none>] [--title <value>] [--description <markdown>] [--description-file <path>] [--due <YYYY-MM-DD>] [--no-due] [--parent <key-or-id>] [--no-parent] [--add-label <name>]... [--remove-label <name>]... [--blocked-by <key-or-id>]... [--unblocked-by <key-or-id>]... [--machine <id-or-name>] [--json]

Arguments:
  <key-or-id>  Task key such as ABC-12 (case-insensitive) or its ULID (required)

Options:
  --status <backlog|todo|in_progress|in_review|done|canceled>  New workflow status; in_review when implementation needs review, done when the criteria are met
  --priority <urgent|high|medium|low|none>  New priority
  --title <value>             New title
  --description <markdown>    Replacement markdown description; use --description-file for long text
  --description-file <path>   Read the replacement description from this UTF-8 file on the invoking machine
  --due <YYYY-MM-DD>          New due date as a calendar date, YYYY-MM-DD
  --no-due                    Clear the due date
  --parent <key-or-id>        New parent task key or id; tasks support at most one level of sub-tasks
  --no-parent                 Promote the task to the top level
  --add-label <name>          Existing label name to add; repeat or comma-separate (repeatable)
  --remove-label <name>       Label name to remove; repeat or comma-separate (repeatable)
  --blocked-by <key-or-id>    Task that must be done before this task; repeat or comma-separate (repeatable)
  --unblocked-by <key-or-id>  Remove this task from the blockers; repeat or comma-separate (repeatable)
  --machine <id-or-name>      Enrolled machine that owns the file paths; defaults to the invoking thread's machine, otherwise the server's
  --json                      Emit machine-readable JSON
  --help, -h                  Show this help and exit

Rules:
  At most one of:  --description, --description-file
  At most one of:  --due, --no-due
  At most one of:  --parent, --no-parent
  --machine        requires --description-file
